# Posted receipt line edit

## Invariant

On a **POSTED** pharmacy receipt, editing a line must apply **all** fields from the request: quantity, unitsInPack, batch, expiry, and prices — then `PharmacyReceiptPostedPriceSync` updates the linked lot and store stock.

## Must

- Use `PharmacyReceiptSupport.applyLine` for both DRAFT and POSTED `updateLine`.
- Pass `previousQuantities` into posted sync when qty may change.
- Keep FE line modal fields editable when `canEditPrices` (draft or posted).

## Must NOT

- Reintroduce `applyPrices` (or any helper that copies old qty/batch/expiry and ignores the request) for POSTED updates.
- Lock qty/batch/expiry in the UI after post (`stockLocked` / `PHARM_RECEIPT_POSTED_FIELD_LOCKED`).
- Treat “save succeeded but values unchanged” as UI-only — that was the old prices-only path.

## Symptom of regression

User edits qty/series/expiry on a posted line, toast says saved, reopen shows previous values.

## Related

Broader lot / movement rules: `.cursor/rules/pharmacy-lot-management.mdc`
(stock only via RECEIPT | OPENING | SALE | RETURN | ADJUSTMENT | TRANSFER).
